  "guards": [
    "Do not assign a numerical duration to 'immediately', 'simultaneously' or the operative-sufficiency standard in clause 3.",
    "The clause 15 24-hour rule is a review deadline, not automatic approval or a 24-hour transmission allowance after approval.",
    "The clause 16 24-hour refusal-notice period starts at the refusal decision, not receipt of the request.",
    "The clause 18 48-hour period starts when NCCCI receives the foreign response, not when the original request was submitted.",
    "Direct subject-to-foreign exchange requires an international treaty that expressly provides for it; otherwise exchange is through NCCCI.",
    "Even during exchange, information is also sent to NCCCI; the NCCCI route is not replaced by peer or foreign transmission.",
    "The 12-hour clause 21 rule concerns information about a KII object of another subject and must not be widened to every received item.",
    "The 24-hour clause 20 rule concerns information initiated by a foreign or international organization.",
    "State-secret information remains subject to Russian state-secret legislation; Order 546 is not a declassification basis."
  ]
